# Recorded model transcripts (M0.4/M0.5) and the checker's own output when
# dogfooding this repo (M7.3) — regenerated per run, not source files.
#
# Named individually rather than ignoring `.acceptance/` wholesale: the
# directory holds input as well as output. `.acceptance/ignore` (#105) is config
# the checker reads and is committed. Judge anything new here on its own merits.
.acceptance/cache/
.acceptance/reviews/
*.local

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# Dogfood runs (`dogfood-logs/`) and `session-state.md` are COMMITTED, not
# ignored. A dogfood run saved with its inputs and its judgement is a candidate
# benchmark case — that is exactly what `tests/fixtures/rating-stability/` is,
# and it could only be turned into one (#190) because those inputs survived.

# Claude handoff notes — rolling, disposable, never committed
handoff*.md
.claude/settings.local.json
